Initialization validates the new configuration before adopting it and then builds the selected method. A configuration that fails validation is not adopted, so an engine that is already running keeps the settings and method it had. Validation follows the same approach as the basket tier. It returns immediately when neither a method nor break-even is enabled and otherwise checks only the settings the selected features read, so a setting that will never be used cannot stop the EA from starting. It rejects a zero or negative ATR multiplier, ladder step or break-even trigger, and a negative ladder lag, minimum step, activation threshold or break-even offset, so the break-even level never sits on the losing side of entry.
