An EA can also supply its own
CTrailMethod
subclass. It creates the method with
new
, hands it over after
Init()
, and the engine deletes it when the engine is destroyed. A method the EA declared as an ordinary object instead is used the same way and is never deleted by the engine. The call has to come after
Init()
, because initialization replaces whatever method the engine holds. The engine applies the same four checks to a supplied method as to the built-in ones.
