Two Clocks in One Tick Handler
The signal is still read once per bar. The new-bar check at the top of
OnTick()
exists to stop one crossover from opening several trades, and that has not changed. A trailing stop manages an existing stop while price continues moving inside the bar. A stop that moves only when a new bar opens can give back the profit from a fast move within the bar, and on a higher timeframe, one bar can cover a large part of the trade.
The trailing call, therefore, goes first in the tick handler, above the new-bar check:
